{"case_id":"C005","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","state","input_semantics","error_path"],"confidence":96,"affected_functions":["numaQuantizeCrossingsByWidth","numaGetCrossingDistances"],"reason":"H0 only decodes bytes with pixReadMem and exercises five PIX color/sharpening transforms. It never constructs a NUMA or directly invokes numaQuantizeCrossingsByWidth, so it does not exercise the newly checked failure state where numaGetCrossingDistances returns nonzero because crossing data is unavailable.","evidence":["S1 assigns the return value of numaGetCrossingDistances to ret and returns ERROR_PTR(\"crossing data not found\", procName, NULL) when ret is nonzero.","The changed path depends on the contents and validity of the NUMA argument nas, plus the parameters supplied to numaQuantizeCrossingsByWidth.","H0's only fuzz-derived object is PIX *pix from pixReadMem(data, size); its subsequent calls are pixModifyHue, pixModifySaturation, pixMosaicColorShiftRGB, pixMultConstantColor, and pixUnsharpMasking.","The readfile.c change only replaces the character literal '\\0' with the equivalent integer value 0 and does not expose a distinct fuzz-worthy semantic gap."],"recommended_action":"Add a harness that derives varied NUMA crossing sequences and quantization parameters from fuzz input, calls numaQuantizeCrossingsByWidth, and covers empty, insufficient, malformed, and valid crossing data, including the nonzero return from numaGetCrossingDistances; destroy every returned NUMA."}
